    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>This plugin integrates your WordPress site with Easybox through the addition of custom components (widgets) for Elementor and Elementor Pro.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Install the plugin directly from the <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/\" rel=\"ugc\">WordPress Plugin Directory</a>.</li>\n<li>Search for the plugin by name (&#8220;easybox&#8221;) and click <strong>Install Now</strong>.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the <strong>Plugins</strong> menu in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Easybox</strong> &#8211;&gt; <strong>Authentication</strong> and login with your Easybox account.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='do%20i%20need%20an%20easybox%20account%20to%20use%20this%20plugin%3F'>\nDo I need an Easybox account to use this plugin?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. While the plugin itself can be activated, its functionalities only work once authenticated with Easybox. Reach out to <a href=\"https://www.easybox.com/en/book-a-demo/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Easybox</a> to obtain your account.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>0.1.2</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial Public Release</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
